  "caption": "Weekend cricket legend Quinn noticed a deep clunk in the shoulder, and the scan report said \"SLAP tear\". Cue reading it 40 times.\n\nSLAP tears show up on scans of many pain-free shoulders, especially after 40, so the finding doesn't always explain the pain. Rehab is usually the first step, over a few months.\n\nWhat can help: building rotator cuff strength, training shoulder-blade control as the arm rises, using hip mobility and trunk rotation if you throw, easing overhead volume for now, and giving it months rather than weeks.\n\nGet it checked if the shoulder locks, becomes suddenly weak after a fall or dislocation, you have constant night pain, fever or weight loss, or you're a young thrower losing speed with a deep ache.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
